<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zulfiqar Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1657">1657</a>–<a href="/years/1713">1713</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Zulfiqar Khan Nusrat Jung</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zulfiqar Khan was a Mughal general and statesman who commanded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>'s armies in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and was appointed the first Nawab of the Carnatic in 1692. He took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gingee">Gingee</a> in 1698. Later he became the most powerful minister at the Mughal court, but after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farrukhsiyar">Farrukhsiyar</a> seized the throne in 1713 he was executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zulfiqar-khan.jpg" alt="Zulfiqar Khan" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jyoti Sardar · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Xulfi_2024.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
